# Story page: thunder
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Thunder Peaks
---
The path climbed into the clouds, and the clouds grumbled about it.

On Thunder Peaks the ground flashes before the sky does. {name} learned to read the flashes the way a sailor reads the sea, which is to say nervously, and with a great deal of swearing.

Inside a ring of scorched stones floated a bubble, perfectly round, perfectly calm. {name} wore it like a hat. The next bolt bounced off it, and so, alarmingly, did the next wall.
